{
  "_comment": "Hand-written, read by the extractor's Rebuild JSON (never shipped; Boss.json carries all of it). dungeons: dungeon -> its final boss as the nameplate shows it (\"???\" = not written yet), or for a dungeon with several loot bosses: boss -> drop names only that boss gives, final boss last (it gets every drop not listed). aliases: in-game location name -> dungeon name, where they differ beyond case, punctuation, a leading 'The' and ': Part ...'. bosses: realm bosses -> positions (spawn spots), Boss Tracker lines (call = regex for the text after \"[<Boss>] \" naming the player fighting it, group 'player'; idle = always present, grey until its spawn line; spawn / defeat = lines that mark it alive / back to idle; portalSeconds = portal time after a defeat; progress = portal opens once every world boss is down; waypoints = extra fixed markers) and, for bosses the wiki does not list, icon / location / type. zones = separate realm regions: a boss located in one is shown only there. pityOnly: boss -> the only drop names its kill adds pity to (it drops more, e.g. Seraph's Domain also drops the earlier bosses' loot; boss not listed = every drop). mobDrops: dungeon -> mob (as its nameplate shows it) -> drop names only that mob drops (written as \"mob\" on those Boss.json drops; a kill of that mob near you adds pity to them). Lines from Melinoe (House-Hades, used with permission).",
